7️⃣Why IDs don’t reset automatically:
When you delete all rows with DELETE FROM users;, the AUTO_INCREMENT counter does not reset. So the next insert continues from the last value (e.g., 14, 15, 16).
This is because databases ensure IDs remain unique over the table’s lifetime and avoid accidental reuse.

To reset IDs to 1, you need:
ALTER TABLE users AUTO_INCREMENT = 1;

    Is it bad practice?

    Not a problem functionally. Your API works perfectly.
    But logging errors for something harmless is not ideal.

